  "divergences": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "The passage assigns each copy to a particular simulated timestep: copy 1 computes step 1, then copy 2 uses that result for step 2, and so on. In `d14`, copies represent depths in a running pipeline. At every tick all copies receive the current input; the first starts again from `N.a4`, and each later copy reads its predecessor's state from the previous tick. Copy k at tick k (numbering from 1) does compute the intended step k, but it also runs at other ticks on other inputs. If run past T ticks, the last copy computes from the most recent T inputs starting from `N.a4`, not from the full history."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean initializes every copy to the original starting state and applies the original readout only to the last copy. These are additional conventions: the passage does not specify initial values for copies awaiting their turn or a readout policy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean covers T = 0, returning the original starting-state readout when there is no last copy. The passage gives no zero-step convention."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Within the `S1` model the construction applies to every network, including already feedforward ones; the passage describes unrolling a recurrent network."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The node copies and predecessor dependencies match the passage, and the intended T-step computation can be followed from copy 1 at tick 1 to copy T at tick T. The declared parallel-update choice nevertheless makes this a repeatedly updated pipeline rather than the passage's sequential evaluation of timestep-specific copies."
}
